                <pb facs="0788" n="656" sameAs="frus:frus1926v01/pg656"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/7887: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-12-01T16:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 1,
                                1926—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received December 1—7:32
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>591. My 589, December 1, 11 a.m. Following from American consul general at
                    Hankow: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“November 30, 11 a.m. Your November 29, 1 p.m. <hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Pope</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic">Truxton</hi> with present
                            force will afford adequate protection. British sloop <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Magnolia</hi> arrived a few days ago and one
                            British destroyer <pb facs="0789" n="657" xml:id="pg657"/> departed, one
                            still here but may leave because of low water. Effort is being made to
                            retain this very secret. Other nations not sending reenforcements.
                            Situation less tense today. Press packers’ and egg packers’ strikes
                            settled yesterday.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
